<section>
  <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.25rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin:0 0 0.6em;max-width:16ch;">
    A user interface, in 150 bytes.
  </h1>

  <p style="max-width:62ch;font-size:1.125rem;color:var(--ink-muted);margin:0 0 2.5rem;">
    EUI delivers application interfaces over HTTPS without HTML, CSS, or JavaScript.
    The server does not send a document to be interpreted; it sends an interface
    tree that is already resolved. Below are the actual bytes for a column
    containing the word <em>Hi</em>, and the thing they draw.
  </p>

  <div class="split">
    <div class="dump">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">0000</td>
            <td class="hex"><span class="op">10</span> 01 02 48 69</td>
            <td class="note"><b>DefAtom</b> interns atom 1 as “Hi”</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">0005</td>
            <td class="hex"><span class="op">11</span> 01 <span class="elide">64 bytes</span></td>
            <td class="note"><b>DefStyle</b> 1, a column with padding 4 on the base surface</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">0047</td>
            <td class="hex"><span class="op">11</span> 02 <span class="elide">64 bytes</span></td>
            <td class="note"><b>DefStyle</b> 2, one step up the text scale, muted foreground</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">0089</td>
            <td class="hex"><span class="op">20</span></td>
            <td class="note"><b>Mount</b> replaces the document</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">008A</td>
            <td class="hex">01 00 01 01 01</td>
            <td class="note">box, id 1, style 1, one child</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="off">008F</td>
            <td class="hex">02 02 02 02 00 01 00</td>
            <td class="note">text, id 2, style 2, holding atom 1</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="render">
      <div class="render__box">Hi</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="caption">
    <span>128 of those bytes are the two style records.</span>
    <span>They are sent once, however many nodes come to use them.</span>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="facts">
  <div class="fact">
    <div class="fact__n">4 619 B</div>
    <div class="fact__what">A 50-row table, sent in full</div>
    <div class="fact__vs">14 362 B as HTML. The structure around the text is 5.3× smaller.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="fact">
    <div class="fact__n">22 B</div>
    <div class="fact__what">One cell changes</div>
    <div class="fact__vs">Reordering fifty keyed rows costs 201 B, because rows move rather than rebuild.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="fact">
    <div class="fact__n">0</div>
    <div class="fact__what">Wakeups while idle</div>
    <div class="fact__vs">Not a setting. There is no render loop in the client to leave running.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;letter-spacing:-0.015em;margin:0 0 0.3em;">What EUI refuses</h2>
  <p style="max-width:62ch;color:var(--ink-muted);margin:0 0 1.5rem;">
    These are not gaps waiting to be filled. Each one is why the client stays small
    enough to audit, and fast enough to be worth the trouble.
  </p>

  <div class="refuse">
    <dl>
      <dt>An open element vocabulary</dt>
      <dd>Fourteen primitive kinds, and the set is closed. Buttons, dialogs and
          tables are composed on the server, which is how the catalogue grows
          without shipping a new client.</dd>

      <dt>The cascade</dt>
      <dd>No selectors, no specificity, no inheritance to resolve. A style is 64
          fixed bytes of already-computed values, so styling a node costs one
          array lookup.</dd>

      <dt>Code from the network</dt>
      <dd>No native code, no JIT, no <code>eval</code>. A local handler is
          bytecode that passes a verifier and runs on a fuel budget, or it does
          not run.</dd>

      <dt>Ambient authority</dt>
      <dd>A capability the manifest never requested has no code path in the
          client. The check is not at the call site; the call site is absent.</dd>

      <dt>Error recovery</dt>
      <dd>A malformed frame ends the session. Tolerance is how a parser becomes
          attack surface.</dd>

      <dt>A fingerprint</dt>
      <dd>No user-agent string, no font enumeration, no canvas readback, no
          device identifier. The client tells a server its viewport and nothing
          else about the person using it.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="margin-top:4rem;max-width:62ch;">
  <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;letter-spacing:-0.015em;margin:0 0 0.75rem;">Where this stands</h2>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);">
    <span class="stamp stamp--built">Built</span>
    The wire format and the session state. <code>eui-proto</code> encodes and
    decodes every construct on this page with no dependencies and no
    <code>unsafe</code>; <code>eui-tree</code> applies the patches, checks
    every reference before placing anything, and enforces the quotas;
    <code>eui-theme</code> resolves roles to colours with contrast met by
    construction; <code>eui-layout</code> places every node with one
    specified algorithm and a list that never measures what it cannot see;
    <code>eui-text</code> shapes with two embedded faces and never reads a
    system font; <code>eui-render</code> draws every one of them as a rounded
    rectangle through one pipeline, and is tested by reading its pixels back;
    <code>eui-client</code> runs the counter end to end over a real socket —
    against a hand-written Rust server, and against <code>soli serve</code>
    itself with the view written in Soli. 160 tests, 46 of them rejection cases.
  </p>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);">
    <span class="stamp stamp--spec">Specified</span>
    The transport, the layout, the theme, the events, the bytecode, and the
    budgets, normatively. The security model is designed on these pages; its
    spec document is still to write.
  </p>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-muted);">
    The window is compiled and not yet run on glass. Every
    number above comes from a test you can run;
    <a href="/docs/budgets">the budgets page</a> names each one.
    If you want the argument rather than the numbers,
    <a href="/docs/overview">start with the overview</a>. If you want to write
    one, <a href="/docs/components">the component reference</a> has the node,
    the style vocabulary, and all 107 builders.
  </p>
</section>

<p class="colophon">
  This site makes no third-party request. Two self-hosted Titillium Web faces,
  124 KB; the monospace is whatever your system already has, because a hex digit
  does not need a downloaded typeface.
</p>
